{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he saw rest, that it was good.</b> He saw that the rest in the perfection of intelligibles, in which the soul finds rest — as it says: וּמִצְאוּ מַרְגּוֹעַ לְנַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם (Jeremiah 6:16) — is the good and the intended end." "<b>And the land, that it was pleasant.</b> He also saw that his land was prepared to yield its produce without toil and to provide sustenance without hardship." "<b>And he bowed his shoulder to bear.</b> Two kinds of burden: the yoke of Torah and the yoke of public service, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Mo'ed Katan 6a): הַאי צוּרְבָא מֵרַבָּנָן דְּאִיתֵיהּ בְּמָתָא כָּל מִילֵי דְמָתָא עָלֵיהּ (any Torah scholar who is in a town — all the town's affairs are upon him)." "<b>And he became a servant of forced labor.</b> The multitude who labor at every kind of work in temporal pursuits became subject to him, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Yoma 72b): that the people of his city were obligated to do his work."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:23.784921663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}